//! Issue 568 unit 8: the cached chains the unit-7 guards' tests in `project::tests` fold, generated from
//! `.scratch/tender-db/568-r208-lots/u7/u7-cache.jsonl.gz` (every in-sample tender's versions and every chain
//! notice's parsed `/v1/notices/{id}/content`, as `g3_port.py` replays them) and, for the out-of-sample 5416534 and
//! 8286472, from `.scratch/tender-db/568-r208-lots/u8-oos/cache_o2` and `cache_o1`.
//!
//! Each notice is reduced to what the lot match and the guards read: the notice section's Tender titles
//! (`TED-TITLE_CONTRACT`, `TED-TITLE`); every lot section (section id and kind as served) with its own `TED-ITEM`,
//! `TED-LOT_NO`, `TED-LOT_NUMBER`, `TED-LOT_TITLE` and `TED-TITLE` values, and its descriptions (`TED-LOT_DESCRIPTION`,
//! `TED-SHORT_DESCR`, `TED-SHORT_CONTRACT_DESCRIPTION`) only where a chain's outcome reads them; every award block
//! (`LotResult`) with the lot references of its subtree, put on the block itself (the projection reads a block's
//! subtree as one, `enclosing`), and its own `TED-CONTRACT_TITLE`, `TED-TITLE_CONTRACT` and `TED-TITLE` values (never
//! an Organization child's). Values are as published, every language, in the store's order; a text value carries
//! its language (`Some("")` for none: the amendment reads titles per language), an id value `None`. The profile is
//! `ted-export-r209` where the notice prints `LOT_NO`, else `ted-export-r208` (the fold reads neither, only that both
//! are legacy).
//!
//! The generator (`gen_568u8a.py`) replays every reduced chain through `g3_port.py`'s amended rule
//! (`apply_amended` with its defaults, FINAL_AMENDED: R1 + R2 included, decision-u7.md "Amendment (unit 8,
//! 2026-10-18)") and checks it gives exactly what the full cached chain gives, block for block. `PORT_*` are those
//! outcomes.

/// One cached value: `(field, language, value)`, the language `Some` for a text value (`""` for none) and `None`
/// for an id.
pub(super) type Value = (&'static str, Option<&'static str>, &'static str);

/// One notice: its Tender titles, then `(section id, [value])` per lot section (with its kind) and per award block.
pub(super) struct Notice {
    pub(super) id: i64,
    pub(super) profile: &'static str,
    pub(super) tender: &'static [Value],
    pub(super) lots: &'static [(&'static str, &'static str, &'static [Value])],
    pub(super) blocks: &'static [(&'static str, &'static [Value])],
}

